---
Guidelines:
- Use NPM dependencies if needed, ensure they are web compatible
- You cannot use websockets. Call devvit_search and query for "realtime" to get more information
- Obey the rules of hooks and only write valid React code

## Visual feedback loop (no Reddit account required)

After meaningful UI changes under `src/client/`, run `npm run ui:capture` and read the PNGs in `src/client/Agent-UI-Viewer/screenshots/` (see `manifest.json` for paths/viewports). Iterate on layout until the screenshots match the spec.

- `npm run dev:ui` — mock API + Vite preview (manual browser at `http://127.0.0.1:7474/inline.html` or `main.html`)
- `npm run ui:capture` — headless Chromium screenshots via Playwright
- `MOCK_SCENARIO=nonmod|empty|mod` — fixture scenario for mock API
- Mock fixtures: `src/client/Agent-UI-Viewer/fixtures.mjs`
- Local dev stubs `@devvit/web/client` via `src/client/Agent-UI-Viewer/stub-devvit-client.ts` (Vite serve only; production build uses the real package)

